ion {:value "2008778"} "Team Sprint, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "2008790"} "Team Pursuit (4,000 metres), Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "2008804"} "Madison, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "2008805"} "Omnium, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "2008868"} "Keirin, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "2008890"} "Team Sprint, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "2008902"} "Team Pursuit (4,000 metres), Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "2008916"} "Madison, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "2008917"} "Omnium, Women"]] [:script {} "$('#same_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#same_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:form {:class "form-inline form-inline-header"} [:select {:name "id", :id "other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "In other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "154649"} "1988"] "\n" [:option {:value "154757"} "1992"] "\n" [:option {:value "154881"} "1996"] "\n" [:option {:value "155011"} "2000"] "\n" [:option {:value "155139"} "2004"] "\n" [:option {:value "258993"} "2008"] "\n" [:option {:value "308200"} "2012"] "\n" [:option {:value "356868"} "2016"] "\n" [:option {:value "19005016"} "2020"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/244"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "Sprint, Women" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "9 – 11 August 2024"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/2178"} "Vélodrome de Saint-Quentin-en-Yvelines, Montigny-le-Bretonneux, France"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/2008812"} "28 from 16 countries"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Format"] [:td {:colspan "2"} "Qualifying over 3½ laps, or 875 metres. Match races over 3 laps, or 750 metres."]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "Of the three medalists at the 2020 Tokyo Games, only the gold medal winner " [:a {:href "/athletes/141388"} "Kelsey Mitchell"] " (CAN) returned to Paris, with neither " [:a {:href "/athletes/147018"} "Olena Starikova"] " (UKR) or " [:a {:href "/athletes/124579"} "Sarah Lee"] " (HKG) featuring on the start list. All three medalists from the UCI Track Cycling World Championships in Glasgow, however, were present, with " [:a {:href "/athletes/151503"} "Emma Finucane"] " (GBR) looking to add Olympic gold to her world title. She faced fierce competition from rivals " [:a {:href "/athletes/143282"} "Lea-Sophie Friedrich"] " (GER) and " [:a {:href "/athletes/145727"} "Ellesse Andrews"] " (NZL)."] "\n\n" [:p {} "A packed field of favorites, that also featured " [:a {:href "/athletes/151508"} "Sophie Capewell"] " (GBR), " [:a {:href "/athletes/142725"} "Mathilde Gros"] " (FRA), and " [:a {:href "/athletes/143279"} "Emma Hinze"] " (GER), all comfortably made it through the qualification round, with rising star " [:a {:href "/athletes/151456"} "Stefany Cuadrado"] " (COL) setting a World junior record with her time of 10.508."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The first three rounds produced little in the way of surprises, with most of the main contenders still in with a chance of a medal. There was disappointment for the home crowd, however, as Mathilde Gros lost her third round heat to " [:a {:href "/athletes/151601"} "Hetty van de Wouw"] " (NED), and then failed to progress via the repêchage."] "\n\n" [:p {} "In the quarter-finals, both Lea-Sophie Friedrich and Emma Finucane won their respective races to advance. The two big casualties came in heats three and four, with Andrews defeating Hinze in two straight races, and van de Wouw doing the same against Capewell."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The first semi-final saw Friedrich lose her first race to van de Wouw, with Friedrich then winning the next two races to advance to the gold medal race. The other semi-final was more one-sided when Andrews beat Finucane without the need for a decider. In the bronze medal final, Finucane beat van de Wouw to win her third medal at the Paris Games. The final saw Ellesse Andrews beat Lea-Sophie Friedrich, with Andrews winning her second gold, and third medal overall, at the velodrome in Paris."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Qualifying"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "R1 Rep"] [:th {} "R2"] [:th {} "Round Two Repêchage"] [:th {} "R3"] [:th {} "Round Three Repêchage"] [:th {} "QF"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "221"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/145727"} "Ellesse Andrews"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/NZL"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/NZL.png"}] "NZL"]] [:td {} "10.108 (3)"] [:td {} "10.671 (1 h3)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "11.271 (1 h3)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "10.917 (1 h3)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "10.746 (1 h3)"] [:td {} "10.565 (1 h2)"] [:td {} "10.685 (1 h1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "166"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/143282"} "Lea-Sophie Friedrich"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GER"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GER.png"}] "GER"]] [:td {} "10.029 (1)"] [:td {} "10.671 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "10.671 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "10.716 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "10.774 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "at 0.014 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "at 0.095 (2 h1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "153"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/151503"} "Emma Finucane"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GBR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GBR.p